/target
.git
.idea
lodestone.toml

# Heavy + machine-specific frontend artifacts. node_modules in
# particular contains symlinks that Docker can't ship through the
# build context on Windows. Stage 1 of the Dockerfile runs `npm ci`
# inside the container, so we don't need the host's node_modules.
frontend/node_modules
frontend/.output
frontend/.nuxt

# Top-level markdown files (README, CONTRIBUTING, etc.) aren't
# COPYed by the Dockerfile. This pattern matches only top-level
# files — docs/*.md is still shipped because the Dockerfile's
# `COPY docs ./docs` does include_str!()-needed files.
*.md
